    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: The object is to win the last (fifth) trick of each hand. There are no trumps. The player who wins the last trick scores points: 3 if the winning card is a 6, 2 if a 7, and 1 if 8 or higher. The session continues for as long as players wish with no fixed target score.',
      "Turn-flow example: Player to dealer's left leads any card. Others must follow suit if possible; if not, any card. Highest card of the suit led wins the trick. Cards stay in a face-up pile. Trick winner leads to the next trick. Five tricks per hand. Winner of the last trick scores: 3 points if winning card is a 6, 2 if a 7, 1 if 8 or higher. Winner of the hand deals the next hand.",
      'Scoring example: Winner of the last trick scores: 3 points if the winning card is a 6, 2 if a 7, 1 if 8 or higher. No fixed target; session continues as players wish. When played for money, winner is paid 1, 2 or 3 stakes by each other player. Win the last (fifth) trick; score 3, 2 or 1 point depending on the winning card (6, 7, or 8+)..',
